From 14f6e83cb865ba21bc6894318888f11c870e337d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Wed, 8 Jul 2026 15:48:08 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] patch 0268 -- #17 diag: load-band audio-underrun probe
 (LOADBAND_STAT) for the rc5 screech A/B

Opt-in diagnostic (default-OFF, SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_LOADBAND_STAT=1) that witnesses
the PicoGUS-SB cave-transition screech fix. The rc5 fix is SDL-side (sdl-engine
SDL/0119 folds a Pixtone-channel quiesce into SDL_DOSAudioFlushRingSilence,
gated by its own SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_FLUSH_QUIESCE_PIXTONE lever); this probe just
records the load-band audio state so the A/B has a log witness alongside the ear.

A LoadBandStatGuard RAII object declared at load_stage entry RIGHT AFTER the
0267 SDL_DOSAudioFlushRingSilence() call: ctor snapshots the POST-flush baseline
(SB IRQ fire count, ISR producer/enqueue cursor, Pixtone-active count) + a
SDL_GetTicks timer; dtor (all return paths) re-reads and emits one line per cave:
  [loadband-stat cave=N dur_ms=D pix_active_entry=P irq_delta=A ring_write_delta=B irq_expected=E]
with E = D/46 (the healthy 512-frame autoinit IRQ period at 11025 Hz). The
discriminator is pix_active_entry: 0 when the flush-quiesce ran (fix ON), >0 when
FLUSH_QUIESCE_PIXTONE=0 skipped it (fix OFF, an SFX still resident in the ring).

Gated by LOADBAND_STAT ALONE -- independent of both LOADSTAGE_SILENCE (0267) and
the SDL FLUSH_QUIESCE_PIXTONE lever -- so BOTH A/B cells emit. No fix logic, no
pump, the 0267 call is unchanged (honors the no-slowdown guardrail). Zero-cost
when off (cached bool -> ctor/dtor no-op); ships in v1.6.2 dormant, not stripped
post-validation (stripping would change the binary + force a re-validate).

Counters via SDL/0119: doskutsu_audio_irq_count (bare extern, core header not on
the nx include path -> declared here), SDL_DOSAudioIsrRingWrite() getter
(SDL_dosaudio_pump.h, already included), g_dos_pixtone_active_count (public
SDL_dospixtone.h, now included). Types verified against the SDL headers.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
